# OS sync on global change (HARD)

**When any edit touches more than one customer-facing surface**, do not leave the OS docs stale.

Surfaces include: `shopify-build/templates/**`, `shopify-build/sections/**` (shared chrome), header/footer groups, nav menus, hub Locked cards, canonical URLs, or approved copy that appears on multiple pages.

## Required forward updates

1. **`planning/m4-section-freeze.md`** — short forward note of what changed (CURRENT MESSAGE wins; never restore an older freeze over the ask).  
2. **`planning/page-template-registry.md`** — if handle, template file, Admin suffix, Locked mock, or QA path changed (or a dead URL was retired/added).  
3. **Nav / decisions** — if URLs or customer-facing copy changed: update the relevant nav spec and/or `planning/10-decision-log.md` / `docs/10-DECISIONS.md` as appropriate.  
4. **Hub** (`docs/index.html`) — only when Andrew says **`LOCK THIS` + URL** (or equivalent) in the **current** message; never flip Locked cards silently.

## Page work

Auto-invoke **`barreletics-page-qa`** and read the registry row **before** editing a page template. **One page per turn.**

## Forbidden

- Shipping a template without updating the registry when the mapping changed  
- Linking dead handles (`/blogs/journal`, `/pages/help`, open/closed/outdoor collection 404s)  
- “Fixing drift” by restoring older freeze/registry rows — fix forward or ASK  
- Pushing theme without Andrew naming a theme ID in the current message

